{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSectorMeasure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSectorMeasure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.OcneanuWeightBranching","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.TwoRowSYTBallot"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.sector_sum_at_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.sector_sum_at_one","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SpinSectorMeasure.lean#L134-L136","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.qint_numerator_eq_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.qint_numerator_eq_sum","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SpinSectorMeasure.lean#L112-L132","doc":"**The classical limit `q = 1`** of the sector weight, stated without dividing by `q − q⁻¹`:\n`[j]_q → j`, so `W_(n−k,k)(1) = (n − 2k + 1)/2ⁿ`. Here: the numerator\n`(q^j − q^{−j})/(q − q⁻¹)` is the sum `∑_{i<j} q^{j−1−2i}`, which at `q = 1` is `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.markovMeasure_twoRow_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.markovMeasure_twoRow_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SpinSectorMeasure.lean#L96-L110","doc":"**The Markov measure on the two-row shape `(m, k)` at convention D.**\n\n`f^(m,k) · W_(m,k) · (q − q⁻¹) · [2]^{m+k} = m_k(m+k) · (q^{d+1} − q^{−(d+1)})`, i.e.\n`μ_(n−k,k) = m_k(n) · [n − 2k + 1]_q / [2]_qⁿ`: the spin-`(n−2k)/2` sector's share of the quantum\ndimension of `n` qubits. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.ocneanuWeight_twoRow_conventionD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.SpinSector.ocneanuWeight_twoRow_conventionD","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/SpinSectorMeasure.lean#L67-L94","doc":"**The two-row Ocneanu weight at convention D is `[n − 2k + 1]_q / [2]_qⁿ`.**\n\nStated with the denominators cleared:\n`W_(m,k) · (q − q⁻¹) · (q + q⁻¹)^{m+k} = q^{d+1} − q^{−(d+1)}`, `d = m − k`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}